  "issue": 392,
  "request": "Goal: Treat absence of tests as an explicit valid flow state instead of a broken test setup. Scope: Update test-execute, downstream test-result-review/retro artifact handling, final-regression classification, schemas, and post-hook promotion so no spec-local tests or no project regression command can be recorded as skip/not applicable when justified by project configuration and spec requirements. Out of Scope: Do not hide real test command failures or missing files unrelated to the no-tests state. Description: Issue #392 reports ENOENT for missing.test.js when testable requirements have zero spec-local tests, invalid_project_test when no project-level regression command exists, and downstream artifact contracts that assume execution. The flow should mechanically validate and promote explicit no-tests artifacts.",
